      "id": "13697",
      "body": "I ran a live check across all the storefront URLs. Current state on the PWA side:\n- Dev — ✅ Live & Serving\n- Test — ✅ Live & Serving\n- SIT — ✅ Deployed Today, Live & Serving. SIT MRT is done on the PWA side.\n- UAT — ✅ Live & Serving\n- Staging — Not Deployed Yet\n- Prod — Not Deployed Yet\nSo we're all deployed except Staging and Prod. Verified by hitting each environment directly, dev/test/sit/uat return the full storefront; staging  prod are still on the MRT default page.\n \nRelease Process:\n- Cut the first release branch (`release/v0.1.0`) and configured branch protection - release branches now require the SIT quality gate to pass before anything can merge.\n- Going with the tag-based promotion approach. It doesn't block the branch or SIT deploys (both done).\nOne honest flag: the automated SIT gate still needs a Lighthouse CI server  a P0 test to go fully green - so for now SIT deploys are manual (that's how today's went). Not blocking progress.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
        "name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
