    {
      "id": "13746",
      "body": "Hi User:557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d reassigning this ticket to you for the SFCC action item to fix the error code 412. Also pending to confirm is the Currency display and the URL link for US Intl storefront.\n\nAdding comments from Gelo’s analysis on the API related issues \n\n✅ Safe To Ignore\n\n- Contentful 400s — CMS has no content types published yet (separate setup work, SFCC-319). Not a PWA bug.\n- Shopper-context 404 on dev — normal for a brand-new session, nothing saved yet.\n\n🟡 Known Cause, Fix Ready, Holding Off On Purpose\n\n- Einstein 400 (wrong site ID) — found the real fix, tested it, works. But the \"working\" value turns out to be a generic Salesforce demo credential, not our own — so not shipping it. Real Einstein setup is already tracked (SFCC-112).\n- Missing translation console warning — real but cosmetic, users see the right text either way. Easy fix, just not done yet.\n\n🔴 Needs Business Manager Access\n\n- Shopper-context 412 on test, sit, and uat (not just test) — traced to the exact SFCC setting: the \"ShopperContextEnabled\" feature toggle is off on those three orgs. It's on for dev. Someone with BM access just needs to flip it on for test/sit/uat to match.",
